## Architecture

- [ ] Pattern chosen: BFF / same-domain session / token-mediating backend /
      browser-based client. Reason recorded below.
- [ ] Sensitive or regulated data uses a BFF or same-domain session.
- Reason:

## Flow

- [ ] Authorization code flow with PKCE `S256`; implicit and password grants
      are not configured at the provider.
- [ ] `state` and `nonce` are generated per attempt and verified.
- [ ] Redirect URIs are exact; no wildcards.
- [ ] Callback removes code and state from the URL and history.
- [ ] Post-login `returnTo` accepts only same-origin relative paths.
- [ ] Issuer is verified on callback when the provider returns `iss`.

## Tokens and session

- [ ] Storage: HTTP-only cookie (BFF) or in memory. No tokens in
      `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, IndexedDB, URLs, or logs.
- [ ] Access token lifetime: <!-- minutes -->; refresh tokens rotate with
      reuse detection, or the BFF renews server-side.
- [ ] Sender-constrained tokens (DPoP) considered: <!-- yes/no, why -->
- [ ] Renewal is single-flight and coordinated across tabs.
- [ ] Renewal failure shows a signed-out state without redirect loops.

## Cookies and CSRF

- [ ] Session cookie: `Secure`, `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax` or `Strict`,
      `__Host-` prefix, no `Domain` attribute.
- [ ] Unsafe methods require a CSRF token or custom header checked server-side.
- [ ] CORS allows exact origins only; credentials never sent to other origins.

## Authorization and errors

- [ ] Every API route authorizes server-side; UI role checks are display only.
- [ ] 401: one renewal, one retry, then expired-session state.
- [ ] 403: access message, session kept, no retry.
- [ ] Guards run before render (loaders); no protected content flash.

## Logout

- [ ] Clears in-memory tokens, query caches, and user-scoped storage.
- [ ] Ends the server session (POST with CSRF protection).
- [ ] Calls the provider end-session endpoint when single sign-out is required.
- [ ] Propagates to other tabs.

## Script injection defenses

- [ ] Content Security Policy without `unsafe-inline` or `unsafe-eval`.
- [ ] No untrusted HTML rendering; dependencies reviewed.

